==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|vatn}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|is}} {{m|gem-pro|*watōr}}, ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|is}} {{m|ine-pro|*wódr̥}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/vahtn/|lang=is}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|n|vatns|vötn}}

# {{lb|is|uncountable}} [[water]] ([[H₂O]])
#: '''''Vatnið''' er mjög [[tær#Icelandic|tært]].''
#:: The '''water''' is very [[clear]].
# {{lb|is|countable}} a [[lake]], a [[water]]
#: ''Á [[Arnarvatnsheiði]] er [[fjöldi]] '''vatna'''.''
#:: On ''Arnarvatnsheiði'' [there] is a multitude of '''lakes'''.
#* Genesis 1-3 ([http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis+1-3&version=KJV English], [http://www.biblegateway.com/passage/?search=Genesis%201-3&version=ICELAND Icelandic])
#*: ''Guð sagði: „Verði festing milli '''vatnanna''', og hún greini '''vötn''' frá '''vötnum'''.“''
#*:: And God said, Let there be a firmament in the midst of the '''waters''', and let it divide the '''waters''' from the '''waters'''.

====Declension====
{{is-decl-noun-n-s|v|a|tn}}

